# Context

## Background
Task T066 asked for every execution path that evaluates untrusted
patterns or schemas to run behind the bounded schema worker. The
study pipeline was the last unconverted surface: loadProtocol,
loadPhasePlan, compileStudy, the protocol lock trio, both review
loaders, and two CLI helpers constructed SchemaValidator directly.

## Why This Way
Same model as eb271d9 (pack) and 413242b (contract variants): swap
new SchemaValidator(schema).errors(document) for
await validateSchemaInstance(schema, document) from @oal/core. The
loaders were already async-safe by contract ("never throws on
content"), so widening them to promises carried through cleanly.

## Gotchas
- The async cascade reaches exported test fixtures (twoCellStudy in
  @oal/study, fixtureStudy in @oal/scheduler); every downstream test
  helper that touches them became async.
- Test files that validate documents our own code produced keep the
  synchronous validator: run.test.ts, analyze.test.ts, events,
  studyrun, schedule fixtures.
- docs/security.md already lists study loading as a routed surface;
  no doc change needed here.
